<section class="business-section" id="signals">
  <div class="business-wrap">
    <div class="business-section-head">
      <div>
        <span class="business-eyebrow">How I help</span>
        <h2>It usually comes down to three questions.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="business-section-intro">What to build, how to build it, and who builds it with you. I've had to answer all three with my own time and money on the line.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="business-signals">
      <div class="business-signal business-reveal">
        <p class="business-signal-said">What should we actually build?</p>
        <p class="business-signal-did">Founders rarely need more features. They need a direction they can commit to. I've run more than 1,000 customer conversations at Butler AI and made several hard pivots. I know how expensive the wrong direction gets.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="business-signal business-reveal">
        <p class="business-signal-said">Which technical calls are hard to undo?</p>
        <p class="business-signal-did">Architecture, build-versus-buy, and what ships first. I've worked on systems handling tens of millions of events a second and split monoliths without downtime. I help founders make those calls before they become expensive.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="business-signal business-reveal">
        <p class="business-signal-said">How do you turn a few engineers into a team that ships?</p>
        <p class="business-signal-did">Hiring, ownership, and how people work together. I've built interview processes from scratch and helped strong engineers become a team with shared standards. Culture is part of the system, not something you add later.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
